## 10. Limitation of liability

To the maximum extent permitted by applicable law, no Licensor or contributor is liable for direct, indirect, incidental, special, consequential or exemplary loss arising from Covered Software or its Use, including loss of data, business or profits, even if advised of the possibility. This does not exclude liability for fraud, intentional misconduct, gross negligence, death or personal injury, or any other liability to the extent it cannot lawfully be excluded.

## 11. Breach, termination and reinstatement

11.1 The permission granted here terminates automatically when You materially breach a condition of this License. Activities outside the grant, including unauthorized Commercial Use, are not authorized while a cure is sought.

11.2 For a first inadvertent, curable noncommercial compliance breach, such as an omitted notice or source attachment, permission is automatically reinstated when You fully remedy the breach within 30 calendar days after actually receiving a sufficiently specific written notice from a relevant Licensor. To remedy it, correct copies You control, stop noncompliant Distribution, and make reasonable efforts to provide missing notices or source to affected recipients. This reinstatement mechanism does not apply to deliberate breaches, unauthorized Commercial Use or repeated breaches. Other reinstatement requires written permission from the relevant Licensor.

11.3 Reinstatement does not retroactively authorize prohibited activity, extinguish accrued claims or modify third-party licenses. A compliant recipient's permissions are not terminated solely because its distributor breached.

## 12. Duties after termination

12.1 Stop activities dependent on the terminated permission, including running, copying, modifying and distributing the affected Covered Software; disable affected deployments and stop offering downloads under that permission. Delete copies under Your control or return them if reasonably requested, except copies retained solely because of legal recordkeeping duties, dispute evidence or technically unavoidable backups. Retained copies must not be used or redistributed, must be access-restricted, and must be removed in the ordinary backup retention cycle where lawful.

12.2 Do not attempt to delete recipients' lawful copies or independently licensed Third-Party Components. Your independent original material is not forfeited; continued use of a combined work still needs all necessary permissions. A separate valid commercial or other license is governed by its own terms.

12.3 Notices, third-party boundaries, brand limitations, disclaimers, liability provisions, accrued claims and these post-termination duties survive to the extent relevant and lawful. No audit access, telemetry, automatic penalty, assignment of Your code or predetermined damages are imposed.

## 13. Law, disputes, language and version

13.1 This License makes no contractual choice of governing law, exclusive court, or compulsory arbitration. Applicable law and competent forums are determined under otherwise applicable legal rules, including mandatory protections. Separate commercial agreements identify their actual contracting parties and any agreed dispute terms.

13.2 The English license is the operative text. The Chinese explanation is explanatory only; discrepancies must be corrected and do not independently expand grants or restrictions. Mandatory language requirements remain unaffected.

13.3 No automatic adoption of later license versions is permitted. A later version does not retroactively replace rights validly granted for earlier material. This License does not revoke rights already granted by third parties or otherwise.
